From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Filer: Tasks' sidebar instead of the icon rail

The places sidebar was the kit's 88 px "rail": each place drawn as an
icon over a wrapped label. Draw it as Tasks' sidebar, the kit's
"destinations" NavigationSidebar: 224 px on the window frame, with the
kit's classes on the sidebar, its lists and Nautilus' live rows, so
LumaUI owns the row height, inset, gap, hover and selection. GTK's
navigation-sidebar look (its 11 px top padding and inset separators)
is no longer used. The kit takes the list's selection bleed back from
the scroller; Filer's scroller and Trash list sit one box deeper, so
the same margin is stated for them and rows keep the kit's 10 px inset.

Section headings are Tasks' "Lists" heading: title case in the kit's
sidebar heading face under a hairline the sidebar's full width, none
over the first group. Long names still ellipsize in the middle.

As in Tasks, the sidebar always shows where you are: when no place is
the current folder, the deepest place that holds it is selected.

The title row is the kit's 46 px instead of Filer's own 42, and the
desktop sidebar toggle's empty host is hidden with the toggle, so it no
longer adds the header bar's start spacing in front of the window
identity.

On a phone the title island grows into the places at their natural
height: the sidebar's scroller passes its list's height up, so every
place shows instead of a two-row strip.
---
diff --git a/src/nautilus-sidebar-row.c b/src/nautilus-sidebar-row.c
index b9af2e0..7e8f79e 100644
--- a/src/nautilus-sidebar-row.c
+++ b/src/nautilus-sidebar-row.c
@@ -586,8 +586,20 @@ nautilus_sidebar_row_init (NautilusSidebarRow *self)
     gtk_widget_init_template (GTK_WIDGET (self));
 
     gtk_widget_set_focus_on_click (GTK_WIDGET (self), FALSE);
-    gtk_label_set_ellipsize (GTK_LABEL (self->label_widget), PANGO_ELLIPSIZE_NONE);
-    gtk_label_set_wrap (GTK_LABEL (self->label_widget), TRUE);
+
+    /* The kit's SidebarRow (Tasks' rows): its classes, so LumaUI draws the
+     * row; the line's gap is the kit's, not the template's margins. */
+    GtkWidget *line = gtk_widget_get_parent (self->label_widget);
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (GTK_WIDGET (self), "luma-navigation-row");
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (GTK_WIDGET (self), "lumaui-row");
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (GTK_WIDGET (self), "lead-icon");
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (line, "luma-navigation-line");
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (line, "lumaui-row-line");
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (self->start_icon_widget, "lumaui-row-lead");
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (self->start_icon_widget, "lead-icon");
+    gtk_widget_set_margin_end (self->start_icon_widget, 0);
+    gtk_widget_add_css_class (self->label_widget, "lumaui-row-title");
+    gtk_widget_set_margin_end (self->label_widget, 0);
 
     self->file = NULL;
 }
